{"name":"November","hex":"#be7767","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"November","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO, ICAO, ITU & IMO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the letter N.","Signal flag for the letter N."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The eleventh month of the Gregorian calendar, following October and preceding December.","A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/November"}],"entries":[{"title":"November","blocks":[{"text":"November is the 11th and penultimate month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 30 days. November was the ninth month of the calendar of Romulus c. 750 BC. November retained its name when January and February were added to the Roman calendar.\nNovember is a month of late spring in the Southern Hemisphere and late autumn in the Northern Hemisphere. Therefore, November in the Southern Hemisphere is the seasonal equivalent of May in the Northern Hemisphere and vice versa. In Ancient Rome, Ludi Plebeii was held from November 4–17, Epulum Jovis was held on November 13 and Brumalia celebrations began on November 24. These dates do not correspond to the modern Gregorian calendar."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/November","wikidata":"Q125"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Chrysanthemums.jpg/500px-Chrysanthemums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Chrysanthemums.jpg/1280px-Chrysanthemums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Chrysanthemums.jpg/500px-Chrysanthemums.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chrysanthemum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChrysanthemums.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe